  members: [ 'mongo1:27017 SECONDARY', 'mongo2:27017 PRIMARY', 'mongo3:27017 SECONDARY' ]
}
{
  term: Long('3'),
  members: [ 'mongo1:27017 PRIMARY', 'mongo2:27017 SECONDARY', 'mongo3:27017 SECONDARY' ],
  why: 'priorityTakeover'
}
```

The settings are the defaults from the text: a 10-second election timeout and a heartbeat every 2 seconds. The step-down started term 2, and a secondary became primary within the 5 seconds. Here it was mongo2; on your run it may be mongo3, whichever had caught up first. A primary that steps down asks a caught-up secondary to stand at once, so nobody waits out the 10 seconds. Once the 20 seconds were over, mongo1 had caught up and had the higher priority, so it called an election, term 3, and won the role back. `lastElectionReason` says why: `priorityTakeover`. Each election added one to the term, and no member voted twice in one term.

